				<h4><span class="tag blue">Not yet published</span></h4>
					
				<p>When the princess Nausicaä takes the palace laundry to the river, she sets in motion one of the best-loved episodes of the <em>Odyssey</em>. This richly illustrated study starts from that ordinary morning and asks what everyday life looked like in the world Homer described: how clothes were washed and woven, how food was prepared and shared, and how households welcomed guests and strangers.</p>
